  "issue_title": "Harden GitHub leakage URL parsing",
  "issue_body": "**Context**\n\nThis PR correctly broadens the GitHub deep-link classes we scrub, but the matcher is still a regex over broad path segments. As the leakage filter becomes more important to benchmark integrity, we should add focused coverage for URL delimiters, punctuation, and GitHub path variants so future changes do not accidentally over-mask legitimate context or under-mask forward references.\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n\n- [ ] Add tests for common markdown delimiters around GitHub links, including angle brackets and trailing punctuation.\n- [ ] Add tests for GitHub issue, PR, release, tree, blob, and compare URL variants with query strings and fragments.\n- [ ] Confirm bare owner and bare repo URLs remain unmasked.\n- [ ] Refactor the matcher only if needed to keep the behavior readable and maintainable.\n\n**Pointers**: `benchmark/leakage.py`, `strip_forward_refs`, `tests/test_leakage.py`",
